WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.090
In 2025, UK trade equalled
61.3 per cent of GDP.

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.270
The economy depends on it.

3
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.910
Yet official figures show
that, apart from 2020 and 2021,

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.850
the UK has run a trade
deficit every year since 1998.

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:23.070
In 2025, that deficit
was 39.4 billion pounds.

6
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.390
So how can a country that buys more
than it sells still shape world trade?

7
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.670
In this mission, you'll map the
UK's biggest trading partners.

8
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.270
Then you'll put its trade
deals on a timeline,

9
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.210
starting with the EU in 2020.

10
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.110
Your mission: explain how the UK can
shape world trade while buying more than

11
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:43.960
it sells.
